{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification binds each perception outcome to a safe, progress-oriented action, enforcing conservative recovery only when obstacles are detected and maximizing coverage by alternating random_walk and move_forward in clear states. Recovery from obstacles uses short turns, with full_rotate reserved for persistent blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, short turns for obstacle recovery, and rapid return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
